vaultmgr` logs show a genuine TPM-reseal race during the baseos upgrade to `0.0.0-master-479b54b2-kvm-amd64`: right after the controller pushed the new sealed vault key (`00:35:15.650 Re-sealing disk key, Vault Unlocked: false`), the re-seal attempt failed with `Failed to re-seal disk key in TPM checking firmware PCRs before sealing: open [/dev/tpmrm0]: device is not a TPM 2.0`. That left the vault permanently `locked` (\"Vault key unavailable\"), so `nodeagent`'s `timer.vault.ready.cutoff` (300s) kept expiring every 10s (\"Exceeded time for vault to be ready 300 by Ns, rebooting\") until it forced a `BootReasonVaultFailure` reboot at `00:40:48`. On the subsequent boot the vTPM/TPM path worked fine and the vault unlocked normally (`00:42:28 Application Data Store unlocked`), and `baseosmgr` only recorded the failure (`swErr: \"Exceeded time for vault to be ready...\"`, demoting IMGB to `DOWNLOADED`) at `00:42:46–53` — about 30+ seconds *after* evetest's upgrade-wait had already given up at `00:42:13` with \"no failure reason reported by the device.\" So the harness message is simply a race: it polled before the device's own failure record landed.\n\nThis is a distinct mechanism from the other `TestKvmToKRepartitionGeometry` ledger entries (those all failed earlier, in setup, on `evebuild/nightly:10.1.0-kvm-amd64` pull-access-denied before any device existed — unrelated to this run, which got a real device up and into the upgrade reboot). It's also different from the previously logged app-vTPM timeout family (`domainmgr`/`vtpmd` `context deadline exceeded` races) and from the `TestVaultKeyModeRecoveryOnExt4` PCR-bank-disabled legacy-key bug — this is the first time this specific host-TPM \"`/dev/tpmrm0`: device is not a TPM 2.0\" re-seal failure during a baseos upgrade appears in the ledger, so it looks like a new, not-previously-documented flaky-TPM/vTPM-timing issue rather than a recurring one.","time":{"start":1795132704000,"stop":1795133544340,"duration":840340}}